# The control sidecar's env (control_sidecar.py) — gitignored as *.local.*.
# MODAL_TOKEN_ID / MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET: the workspace token the modal SDK
# reads natively. It carries deploy/delete rights and stays OUT of the app's
# runtime env, which only ever holds the proxy token (wk-….ws-…). Mint it WITHOUT
# writing ~/.modal.toml and WITHOUT printing it: README.md, "Running it", has the
# block that mints into a private directory and copies the two values here.
# This file is the sidecar's own: mode 600, read by no other service.
MODAL_TOKEN_ID=''
MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=''
# The bearer the APP presents to the sidecar (MODAL_CONTROL_TOKEN on the app
# side). Not the Modal token; the sidecar refuses to start without one. Under
# compose it is NOT set here: the compose service reads it from the root .env, so
# the app and the sidecar share one value.
MODAL_CONTROL_TOKEN=''
# Bind address. Defaults shown: loopback, for a laptop run. The compose service
# sets MODAL_CONTROL_HOST itself, inside its own container only.
MODAL_CONTROL_HOST='127.0.0.1'
MODAL_CONTROL_PORT='8124'
# App names, as ops.py reads them. Defaults shown.
HAMES_MODAL_APP_NAME='hames-small-models'
HAMES_MODAL_27B_APP_NAME='hames-private-27b'
